750:
The city makes the following findings:
(1) It is within the power of municipal corporations to establish ambient air quality standards not less stringent than those provided by the federal and state laws governing air pollution control;
(2) It is further within the power of municipal corporations to regulate the handling of solid wastes generated and collected within their jurisdiction and to impose certain restrictions upon the burning of yard trimmings which heretofore may have been collected and disposed of at municipal solid waste disposal facilities;
(3) Major land-clearing activities are temporary in nature and may be permitted under controlled conditions, provided adequate safeguards have been taken to ensure ambient air pollution is minimized; and
